{# The table's bottom edge and its control. It is drawn whenever there are
   rows, whether or not there is a page either side of this one — without it
   the last row simply falls off the card.

   It sits under the table's scroll box rather than inside it: the box is
   height-bounded, so the pager is on screen at the foot of it whatever the
   rows are doing, and a control stuck over its own table needed a rule of its
   own to say it was not one.

   It counts nothing. `20 events` under a page of twenty is a fact about a
   window, and the card's own caption already says how many events every filter
   on the page selects.

   Newer and Older, not Previous and Next. The list is newest first and the
   cursor walks it: `direction=backward` from the top of the page reaches the
   events that arrived after these, and `forward` reaches the ones before. An
   operator paging a stream is asking about time, not about the ordinal of a
   page, and `Previous` on a newest-first list points at whichever of the two
   the reader guessed — which is exactly the wrong thing for a control that
   moves a triage window. `rel` still says prev and next, because that is what
   they are to a browser.

   Both directions are always drawn, joined into one control: a footer that
   renders only the link it has moves the other one across the row the moment
   the first appears, so the button an operator is aiming at is somewhere else
   on the next page. The direction there is no page in is the same object,
   disabled.

   Extra small, on a strip barely taller than the buttons: this is the quietest
   control on the card, it is read once at the end of a page, and every pixel
   it takes is a pixel of rows on a screen whose whole subject is rows. #}
<nav class="flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center border-t border-base-300 px-4 py-1" aria-label="Pagination" data-testid="do-pager">
  <div class="join" data-testid="do-pager-links">
    {% if params.previousHref %}
      <a class="btn btn-xs join-item" rel="prev" href="{{ params.previousHref }}" data-testid="do-pager-newer">← Newer</a>
    {% else %}
      <span class="btn btn-xs join-item btn-disabled" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="do-pager-newer-disabled">← Newer</span>
    {% endif %}
    {% if params.nextHref %}
      <a class="btn btn-xs join-item" rel="next" href="{{ params.nextHref }}" data-testid="do-pager-older">Older →</a>
    {% else %}
      <span class="btn btn-xs join-item btn-disabled" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="do-pager-older-disabled">Older →</span>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</nav>
